  "id": "restraint",
  "term": "restraint",
  "definition": "Restraint is described here as a staff-led decision event during a behavioral crisis, not just an isolated act. In this view, whether restraint happens is shaped by the surrounding context, staff thinking, and organizational conditions created by leadership, with outcomes feeding back into later practice.",
